.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/escape-string-regexp Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "escape-string-regexp [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/escape-string-regexp.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/escape-string-regexp)"
.PP
.RS 4
Escape RegExp special characters 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install escape\-string\-regexp
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const escapeStringRegexp = require('escape\-string\-regexp');

const escapedString = escapeStringRegexp('How much $ for a 🦄?');
//=> 'How much \\\\$ for a 🦄\\\\?'

new RegExp(escapedString);
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can also use this to escape a string that is inserted into the middle of a regex, for example, into a character class\&.

.PP
